   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello.  I&#39;m trying to figure out how to estimate one model in lavaan, then constrain the loadings in a subsequent model to equal those from the first.  I&#39;m able to extract the parameters from model 1 and save them as values, but then lavaan doesn&#39;t recognize those values in model 2.  Any guidance would be great, and sorry if I&#39;m duplicating anything.<div><br></div><div><div>############################################################</div><div>#SAVE LOADINGS</div><div>############################################################</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>m0 &lt;- &#39;     f=~ y1 + y2 + y3 + y4</div><div>        </div><div>          &#39;</div><div>m0result &lt;- sem(m0, data=d)<br></div><div>summary(m0result)</div><div><br></div><div>coeff&lt;-lavInspect(m0result, &quot;est&quot;)<br></div><div>coeff&lt;-coeff$lambda</div><div><br></div><div>l1&lt;-coeff[1,1]</div><div>l2&lt;-coeff[2,1]</div><div>l3&lt;-coeff[3,1]</div><div>l4&lt;-coeff[4,1]</div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div><div>############################################################</div><div>#APPLY LOADINGS</div><div>############################################################</div><div><br></div><div>#NOTE - trying to get l1-l4 below to equal l1-l4 from above</div><div><br></div><div># check simulation using obs scores, binary t</div><div>m2 &lt;- &#39;     f=~ l1*y1 + l2*y2 + l3*y3 + l4*y4</div><div>            f ~ r + rz + t</div><div>            t ~ z + r + rz</div><div>            f~~t</div><div>            </div><div>            </div><div>          &#39;</div><div><br></div><div>m2result &lt;- sem(m2, data=dbw, ordered=c(&quot;t&quot;))</div><div>summary(m2result)</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
